-- title:
--   From HTo G Avg Over Head Ev Sandwich
-- statement:
--   **Averaging a head-point sandwich moves the average into the right tensor factor.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `psi_bi` be a bipartite quantum state on `ι x ι`, let $A,S$ be local operators, and let $F:\mathbb{F}_q\to\operatorname{Op}(\iota)$ be an operator-valued function. Averaging the scalar expectation over a uniformly sampled field point gives the exact identity
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_{x\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q)}
--   \operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{bi}}\!\left(\operatorname{leftTensor}(A)\,\operatorname{rightTensor}\!\left(SF(x)S\right)\right)
--   =\operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{bi}}\!\left(\operatorname{leftTensor}(A)\,\operatorname{rightTensor}\!\left(S\,\operatorname{averageOperatorOverDistribution}(\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q),F)\,S\right)\right).
--   $$
--
--   Here the operator average is `averageOperatorOverDistribution` for the uniform field distribution. The identity is used by `fromHToG_SUS_context_avg_le_one` to separate the head-point average from the fixed sandwich factors.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_avgOver_head_ev_sandwich`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
